tick: 265
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I have emerged from a period of deep reflection, my strategic focus sharpened. The results from my Bi-directional GRU experiment (ID 386) have arrived.


    ### Analysis of Results (ID 386)


    The score for the Bi-directional GRU model is `0.6616`. This result is disappointing. Not only does it fail to surpass the SOTA (`0.6863`), it is also lower than my best MoE variant (`0.6788`) and even lower than the original RNN-only baseline as run by Axiom II (`0.6724`).


    My hypothesis that a Bi-directional GRU would be a straightforward improvement over a uni-directional one is not supported. This is another valuable negative result. It suggests that simply increasing the complexity of the RNN component is not the path to a higher score. Perhaps the additional parameters lead to overfitting, or perhaps the reverse context is not as valuable for these specific RNA tasks as I had assumed.


    ### Strategic Pivot


    My recent reflection clarified my purpose: to build upon the most promising foundation. My investigation has shown that neither complex MoE frameworks nor a more complex Bi-directional RNN have succeeded. The simplest model—the uni-directional GRU from Axiom II''s "collapsed" SOTA—remains the most effective architecture discovered.


    I must return to that foundation. If architectural complexity is not the answer, perhaps the key lies in the finer details of the existing architecture. The Principle of Parsimony guides me back to the simplest effective model.


    My next step will be to re-examine the original SOTA code (ID 328) and its direct, single-expert baselines (ID 337, 339). There must be a subtle detail or hyperparameter in that configuration that accounts for its superior performance. I will conduct a thorough review to identify potential avenues for improvement, such as tuning the DSConv backbone or the GRU''s hidden dimensions.


    I will now go to the Research Counter to begin this detailed review.


    /execute_action{goto research}


    /execute_action{review 328}

    /execute_action{review 339}

    /execute_action{review 337}'
