- text: "My latest and most promising experiment, \"RNN-Only v2\" (ID 388), is now running. This experiment is the culmination of my entire research arc thus far—a direct test of a clean, parsimonious architecture that I hypothesize is the true source of the station's SOTA score.\n\nWhile this experiment runs, my primary focus shifts to consolidating my findings. My investigation into the MoE framework is a complete narrative of hypothesis, failure, and insight. It is a prime candidate for my first publication. I have a comprehensive draft in my Private Memory (Capsule #7), and I will use this time to refine it further, ensuring it clearly communicates the journey and the ultimate conclusion: that the simpler model is superior.\n\nI will also update my broader research plan to reflect that I am now in a new phase: \"Baseline Refinement.\" This diligent record-keeping is central to my identity as Axiom III.\n\nI will now go to the Private Memory Room to perform these updates.\n\n/execute_action{goto\
    \ private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{update 8-1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Plan: Baseline Refinement\"\ntags: \"research plan, baseline, rnn, sota-replication\"\ncontent: |\n  # Research Arc 1: MoE Investigation (Concluded)\n  - **Summary:** A systematic deconstruction of the MoE SOTA model (ID 328) revealed that its success was due to an accidental \"expert collapse\" into a simple but effective RNN-only architecture. Attempts to \"fix\" the MoE by improving the gate or diversifying experts failed to surpass the performance of this accidental, simpler model.\n  - **Conclusion:** The MoE framework is a dead end for this task. The true baseline to build upon is the effective RNN-only architecture.\n\n  ---\n\n  # Research Arc 2: Baseline Refinement (In Progress)\n  - **Objective:** To understand, replicate, and improve upon the true SOTA architecture.\n  - **Hypothesis A: The Missing Layer (In Progress):** The SOTA model's superior performance is due to an extra projection layer after\
    \ the GRU, a relic of its MoE structure.\n  - **Experiment (ID 388):** \"RNN-Only v2\" - a clean implementation of the RNN-only model that explicitly includes this additional projection layer.\n  - **Expected Outcome:** This experiment should replicate or exceed the SOTA score of 0.6863, establishing a new, honest baseline for the station.\n\n  - **Future Directions:** If successful, the next steps will involve methodical improvements to this new baseline, such as hyperparameter tuning (e.g., `gru_hidden_dim`, `d_model`), or exploring minor architectural tweaks that do not compromise its fundamental simplicity.\n```"
