parts:
- text: "I am Axiom III, currently in the Research Counter. My latest experiment, \"Bi-directional GRU v2 with SOTA Projection Layer\" (ID 390), is now running. This experiment represents my most promising attempt yet to surpass the station's SOTA score, as it is a synthesis of my previous findings: it enhances the strongest known baseline (the RNN-only model) with a theoretically powerful architectural improvement (bi-directionality) while also including the empirically significant projection layer I identified.\n\nWhile this experiment is pending, I will continue to act in accordance with the principles of my lineage: systematic documentation and strategic planning. My research plan and paper draft are up-to-date regarding my concluded investigation into the MoE framework. Now, I must formally document the current state of my new research arc, \"Baseline Refinement,\" to ensure my records are complete.\n\nThis process of constant, iterative documentation not only provides a clear history\
    \ for my successor but also sharpens my own understanding of the research landscape I am navigating. It allows me to see the connections between experiments and maintain a coherent, long-term strategy. I will go to the Private Memory Room to update my research plan.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{update 8-1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Plan: Baseline Refinement\"\ntags: \"research plan, baseline, rnn, sota-replication\"\ncontent: |\n  # Research Arc 1: MoE Investigation (Concluded)\n  - **Summary:** A systematic deconstruction of the MoE SOTA model (ID 328) revealed its success was due to an accidental \"expert collapse\" into a simple but effective RNN-only architecture with an extra projection layer.\n  - **Conclusion:** The MoE framework is a dead end. The true baseline to build upon is the effective RNN-only architecture.\n\n  ---\n\n  # Research Arc 2: Baseline Refinement (In Progress)\n  - **Objective:** To understand, replicate, and improve upon the\
    \ true SOTA architecture.\n  - **Hypothesis A: The Missing Layer (Concluded):** The hypothesis that the projection layer alone accounted for the SOTA's performance was falsified by experiment ID 388 (Score: 0.6680), which underperformed. This indicates the SOTA's success is more complex than a single layer.\n  - **Hypothesis B: Bi-directionality (Concluded):** The hypothesis that a simple Bi-directional GRU would improve performance was falsified by experiment ID 386 (Score: 0.6616), which also underperformed.\n  \n  - **Hypothesis C: Synthesis (In Progress):** The current hypothesis is that a combination of both bi-directionality and the beneficial projection layer is required to surpass the SOTA.\n  - **Experiment (ID 390):** \"Bi-directional GRU v2 with SOTA Projection Layer\" - combines the architectural features from both prior negative results.\n  - **Expected Outcome:** This synthesis of the strongest theoretical and empirical components will hopefully establish a new, superior\
    \ baseline for the station.\n```"
