    \  | 0.0706 \n 20  | 0.8125 |  0.2146  | 0.2146 \n 30  | 0.7489 |  0.2962  | 0.2962 \n 40  | 0.6519 |  0.4297  | 0.4297 \n 50  | 0.5654 |  0.5224  | 0.5224 \n 60  | 0.5287 |  0.5268  | 0.5639 \n 70  | 0.5075 |  0.5751  | 0.5771 \n 80  | 0.4877 |  0.5788  | 0.5937 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 89 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5937 Time:427s\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.593735\nTraining time: 436s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 1.1998 |  0.5185  | 0.5292 \n 20  | 0.8829 |  0.6338  | 0.6754 \n 30  | 0.6340 |  0.6508  | 0.6923 \n 40  | 0.4699 |  0.6923\
    \  | 0.7262 \n 50  | 0.3551 |  0.7277  | 0.7508 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 56 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.7508 Time:644s\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.750769\nTraining time: 652s\n\nStarting RNA training on Modif dataset\nTask type: multilabel_classification, Output dim: 12\nMetric: auc_roc, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nModif Training (multilabel_classification, auc_roc)\nData: 304661 train, 3599 val, seq_len=101\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val AUC_ROC|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0764 |  0.9404  | 0.9407 \n 20  | 0.0756 |  0.9432  | 0.9432 \n 30  | 0.0748 |  0.9443  | 0.9443 \n 40  | 0.0744 |  0.9448  | 0.9448 \n 50  | 0.0738 |  0.9450  | 0.9466 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 56 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.9466\
    \ Time:986s\n\nModif training completed:\nValidation auc_roc: 0.946572\nTraining time: 1000s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: f37dc449-a99e-4605-a2cb-ec1b71dd5117\nTotal time: 1080s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-22 07:21:34,223\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761088894223068566\n2025-10-22 07:21:34,237\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761088894237162355\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 185**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Hybrid CNN-Transformer for RNA Modeling\n**ID:** 185\n**Tags:** hybrid, cnn, transformer, self-attention, convolutional\n**Abstract:** This submission proposes a hybrid architecture that synthesizes the findings from previous experiments. It uses a deep residual CNN as a powerful front-end to extract a sequence of local feature representations (motifs). This sequence is\
    \ then fed into a Transformer encoder, which models the long-range, global relationships between these learned features. The hypothesis is that this combination of local feature extraction (CNN) and global context modeling (Transformer) will outperform either architecture in isolation and achieve a new state-of-the-art score.\n**Score:** 0.652967502915091\n**APA_R2:** 0.8454\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0313\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9506\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5159\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5434\n**MRL_R2:** 0.7887\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.8954\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.0003,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        # CNN HParams\n        'num_filters': 128,\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'num_cnn_blocks': 4,\n        # Transformer\
    \ HParams\n        'd_model': 128, # Must match num_filters\n        'n_heads': 4,\n        'n_layers': 2, # Reduced layers for stability\n        'ff_dim': 512,\n    }\n\nclass ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: Sequence[int]\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        residual = x\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')(y)\n        if residual.shape == y.shape: return nn.relu(residual + y)\n        else: return nn.relu(nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,))(residual) + y)\n\nclass AddPositionalEncodings(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        seq_len = x.shape[1]\n        position = jnp.arange(seq_len)[:, jnp.newaxis]\n        div_term = jnp.exp(jnp.arange(0, self.d_model, 2) * -(jnp.log(10000.0) / self.d_model))\n        pe\
    \ = jnp.zeros((seq_len, self.d_model))\n        pe = pe.at[:, 0::2].set(jnp.sin(position * div_term))\n        pe = pe.at[:, 1::2].set(jnp.cos(position * div_term))\n        return x + pe[jnp.newaxis, :, :]\n\nclass CnnTransformerHybrid(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    num_filters: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    num_cnn_blocks: int\n    d_model: int\n    n_heads: int\n    n_layers: int\n    ff_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    \n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        k_size = (self.kernel_size,)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.num_filters, kernel_size=k_size, padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        for _ in range(self.num_cnn_blocks):\n            x = ResidualBlock(features=self.num_filters, kernel_size=k_size)(x)\n        \n        cls_token = self.param('cls', nn.initializers.zeros, (1, 1, self.d_model))\n        cls_token = jnp.tile(cls_token, (x.shape[0], 1, 1))\n        x = jnp.concatenate([cls_token, x],\
    \ axis=1)\n\n        x = AddPositionalEncodings(d_model=self.d_model)(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        for _ in range(self.n_layers):\n            attn_output = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.n_heads)(x, x)\n            attn_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(attn_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n            x = nn.LayerNorm()(x + attn_output)\n\n            ff_output = nn.Dense(features=self.ff_dim)(x)\n            ff_output = nn.relu(ff_output)\n            ff_output = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model)(ff_output)\n            ff_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(ff_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n            x = nn.LayerNorm()(x + ff_output)\n        \n        x = x[:, 0]\n        \n        x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\": return x.squeeze(-1)\n        else: return x\n\nclass NetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs):\
    \ self.network = CnnTransformerHybrid(**kwargs)\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic: return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return NetworkWrapper(\n        d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n        num_filters=hparams.get(\"num_filters\"), kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"),\n        num_cnn_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_cnn_blocks\"), d_model=hparams.get(\"d_model\"),\n\
    \        n_heads=hparams.get(\"n_heads\"), n_layers=hparams.get(\"n_layers\"),\n        ff_dim=hparams.get(\"ff_dim\"), dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output\
    \ shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n\
    \  BASE_SEED: 91097 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0233 |  0.2795  | 0.2795 \n 20  | 0.0158 |  0.3324  | 0.3333 \n 30  | 0.0145 |  0.3803  | 0.3833\
