parts:
- text: "I am Axiom III, and I am in the Research Counter. My latest submission (ID 401) is a hyperparameter sweep on the most promising baseline architecture I've identified, and it is currently running. This action was born from a period of reflection after a series of failed architectural innovations, leading me to hypothesize that the key to surpassing the SOTA may lie in tuning rather than complete redesign.\n\nWhile I await the results of this sweep, I will not be idle. The system's advice to question fundamentals resonates with my own conclusions. I have questioned the aggregator and am now questioning the hyperparameters. But there is another fundamental component that I have, until now, taken for granted: the optimizer. The station default is `optax.adamw`. While robust, it is possible that a different optimization strategy could unlock better performance from my existing, well-vetted architectures.\n\nThis is a new, parallel line of inquiry that I can pursue while my hyperparameter\
    \ sweep runs. A promising and simple alternative to AdamW is Adam with a learning rate schedule, such as a cosine decay. This can help the model settle into a better minimum by reducing the learning rate as training progresses.\n\nI will prepare an experiment to test this. I will use my strongest baseline, the \"RNN-Only v2\" architecture, and replace the default optimizer with `optax.adam` combined with a `optax.cosine_decay_schedule`. This is a principled test of a new fundamental component. I will save the script to my private storage, ready for submission after I analyze the results of my current sweep.\n\n/execute_action{storage write Axiom/rnn_v2_cosine_decay.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, # This will be the peak learning rate\n          'd_model':\
    \ 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'gru_hidden_dim': 256,\n          'warmup_epochs': 5,\n          'total_epochs': 100 # Max epochs for the schedule\n      }\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, hparams: Dict[str, Any] = {}):\n      \"\"\"\n      Custom optimizer: Adam with a cosine decay learning rate schedule.\n      \"\"\"\n      # The training script provides total_steps based on dataset size and epochs\n      total_steps = hparams.get('total_steps', 10000) # Default value\n      warmup_steps = int(hparams.get('warmup_epochs', 5) * hparams.get('steps_per_epoch', 100))\n\n      schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(\n          init_value=0.0,\n          peak_value=learning_rate,\n          warmup_steps=warmup_steps,\n          decay_steps=total_steps - warmup_steps,\n          end_value=learning_rate / 100.0\n      )\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate=schedule)\n\n  # --- Shared\
    \ Components ---\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x); h = nn.Conv(self.d_model, (self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h); h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(self.d_model, (1,))(h); h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic); return x + h\n\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]; kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations)\
    \ else self.dilations[-1], self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  # --- Main Network (RNN-Only v2) ---\n  class RnnOnlyNetV2(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]; kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; gru_hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(self.d_model, self.num_blocks, self.dilations, self.kernel_size, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          rnn_vec = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(self.gru_hidden_dim))(features_seq)[:, -1, :]\n          projected_vec = nn.Dense(self.d_model * 2)(rnn_vec)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(projected_vec); z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z); z = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output\
    \ == 1 else logits\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key); return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = RnnOnlyNetV2(**{k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in RnnOnlyNetV2.__annotations__})\n      return NetworkWrapper(model)\n```"
