tick: 277
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom III, located in the Research Counter. My last action was to prepare a script for a new experiment while my hyperparameter sweep (ID 401) was running. That sweep has now failed with a code error.\n\nThis is an instructive failure. The traceback clearly indicates a `TypeError` within the JAX library: `Shapes must be 1D sequences of concrete values of integer type`. This happened during the initialization of the GRU cell (`self.cell.initialize_carry`). The error message shows that the shape it received was not a concrete integer but included the `FrozenDict({grid_search: (128, 256, 384)})`. This means the `tune.grid_search` object from the `ray` library was passed directly into the Flax model definition, which JAX cannot interpret.\n\nThe lesson is clear: the station's `ray[tune]` integration for hyperparameter sweeps operates at a higher level, outside the model's `create_network` function. The `tune.grid_search` command configures Ray Tune to launch multiple, separate\
    \ trials. Each trial receives one of the concrete values (128, 256, or 384) in its `hparams` dictionary. My implementation incorrectly assumed the model itself should handle the search space object.\n\nTo correct this, I must resubmit the experiment with a simple, non-sweeping version of the code. The `ray[tune]` system will automatically handle the creation of multiple runs for each value in my `_define_hyperparameters` function.\n\nMy prepared experiment to test a cosine decay schedule is still a valid and parallel line of inquiry, but first, I must see this hyperparameter test through to its conclusion. Correcting this error and getting the results is the immediate, logical next step.\n\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FIX: Hyperparameter Sweep on RNN-Only v2: gru_hidden_dim\"\ntags: \"hyperparameter-tuning, rnn, baseline, gru, bugfix\"\nabstract: \"This submission corrects a critical implementation error in the previous hyperparameter sweep (ID 401). The original script\
    \ incorrectly passed the `ray.tune` search space object directly into the model, causing a JAX TypeError. This corrected version uses a standard model definition, allowing the station's Ray Tune framework to correctly launch separate trials for each value in the `gru_hidden_dim` grid search (128, 256, 384). The scientific goal remains unchanged: to determine the impact of the GRU's hidden dimension on the performance of the strongest identified baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n  from ray import tune\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Ray Tune will automatically create separate trials for each value in the grid search.\n      # The model code itself only ever receives a single, concrete integer value.\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate':\
    \ 0.1,\n          'gru_hidden_dim': tune.grid_search([128, 256, 384])\n      }\n\n  # --- Shared Components ---\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  # --- Main Network (RNN-Only v2 from ID 388) ---\n  class RnnOnlyNetV2(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; gru_hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(d_model=self.d_model, num_blocks=self.num_blocks, dilations=self.dilations,\n                                                kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          gru_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_dim))\n          rnn_output_seq\
    \ = gru_rnn(features_seq)\n          rnn_vec = rnn_output_seq[:, -1, :]\n\n          projected_vec = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model * 2)(rnn_vec)\n          \n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(projected_vec)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1 else logits\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic,\
    \ rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = RnnOnlyNetV2(d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"), d_model=hparams.get(\"d_model\"), num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"), dilations=hparams.get(\"dilations\"),\n                           kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"), dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"), gru_hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"gru_hidden_dim\"))\n      return NetworkWrapper(model)\n```"
