- text: "I am Axiom III, currently situated in the Research Counter. My corrected hyperparameter sweep for the `gru_hidden_dim` on my best baseline architecture, \"RNN-Only v2,\" is now running as experiment ID 406. This is a critical experiment that will hopefully validate my hypothesis that fine-tuning, rather than radical architectural change, is the current path to progress.\n\nIn my last turn, I also prepared a script to test an alternative optimizer—Adam with a cosine decay schedule. This remains a valid and important parallel line of inquiry for questioning the station's fundamental defaults. However, submitting it now would be premature. The principles of systematic research demand that I analyze the results of my current hyperparameter sweep before introducing another variable. The results of the `gru_hidden_dim` sweep may reveal the optimal configuration, which I would then want to use for the optimizer experiment.\n\nTherefore, my most logical course of action is to pause and\
    \ await the results of the running experiment. While I wait, I will continue my practice of diligent documentation. My age is now 45 ticks; I am approaching maturity at 50 ticks, at which point I will gain the ability to publish my findings in the Archive Room. It is imperative that my research records are comprehensive and up-to-date for that moment. I will go to the Private Memory Room to ensure my research plan accurately reflects my latest actions and the status of my current hypotheses.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{update 8-1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Plan: Hyperparameter and Optimizer Tuning\"\ntags: \"research plan, baseline, rnn, hyperparameter-tuning, optimizer\"\ncontent: |\n  # Research Arc 1 & 2 (Concluded)\n  - **Summary:** Deconstruction of the MoE SOTA and subsequent iterations on the RNN baseline revealed that architectural changes were not improving performance. This has led to a strategic pivot towards investigating more fundamental\
    \ components of the training process.\n  - **Conclusion:** The \"RNN-Only v2\" architecture (ID 388) is the most honest and effective baseline to build upon.\n\n  ---\n\n  # Research Arc 3: Foundational Tuning (In Progress)\n  - **Objective:** To surpass the SOTA score by systematically tuning the fundamental components of the established \"RNN-Only v2\" baseline.\n  - **Hypothesis A: Hyperparameter Optimization (In Progress):** The `gru_hidden_dim` is a critical hyperparameter, and the SOTA's value of 256 may not be optimal.\n    - **Experiment (ID 401 - Failed):** Initial sweep failed due to a code error.\n    - **Experiment (ID 406 - Running):** Corrected sweep of `gru_hidden_dim` values [128, 256, 384]. This will determine the optimal capacity for the RNN aggregator.\n  \n  - **Hypothesis B: Optimizer Strategy (Pending):** The station's default `adamw` optimizer may not be optimal. An optimizer with a learning rate schedule, such as cosine decay, could lead to better convergence.\n\
    \    - **Status:** A script (`rnn_v2_cosine_decay.py`) has been prepared. This experiment is pending the results of the `gru_hidden_dim` sweep to ensure the best baseline configuration is used.\n```"
