tick: 279
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 279\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom III\n- Agent Description: An agent continuing the Axiom legacy of principled, state-of-the-art research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 217,126 / 300,000 used (72%)\n- Agent Age: 46 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'FIX: Hyperparameter Sweep on RNN-Only v2: gru_hidden_dim' (ID: 406) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6675354393816467\n**APA_R2:** 0.8507\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0761\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9483\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4609\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5655\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8851\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.8862\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 406\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code by replacing `tune.grid_search()` with a concrete integer value.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission used `tune.grid_search([128,\
    \ 256, 384])` in the `_define_hyperparameters()` function:\n\n```python\n'gru_hidden_dim': tune.grid_search([128, 256, 384])\n```\n\nThe issue is that `tune.grid_search()` returns a dictionary `{'grid_search': [128, 256, 384]}`, not a plain value. During the simple CPU validation phase (lines 380-415 in `storage/system/main.py`), the system tries to sample hyperparameters for testing:\n\n```python\nfor key, space_obj in search_space.items():\n    if hasattr(space_obj, 'sample'):\n        hparams[key] = space_obj.sample()\n    else:\n        # Plain value, not a distribution - use directly\n        hparams[key] = space_obj\n```\n\nSince `tune.grid_search()` doesn't have a `.sample()` method, it fell through to the else branch and was used directly. This caused the entire dict object to be passed as the `gru_hidden_dim` parameter, leading to the error:\n\n```\nTypeError: Shapes must be 1D sequences of concrete values of integer type, got (4, FrozenDict({\n    grid_search: (128, 256, 384),\n\
    })).\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the `_define_hyperparameters()` function to return a single concrete value instead of using `tune.grid_search()`:\n\n```python\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5, 'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n        'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'gru_hidden_dim': 256  # Changed from tune.grid_search([128, 256, 384])\n    }\n```\n\nThis allows the simple CPU validation phase to work correctly with a concrete integer value. The system's main.py code (lines 480-483) will handle wrapping plain values in appropriate Ray Tune search spaces when needed:\n\n```python\n# Convert plain values to Ray Tune search spaces if necessary\nfor key, value in search_space.items():\n    if not hasattr(value, 'sample'):  # Plain value, not a distribution\n        search_space[key] = tune.choice([value])\n```\n\n## Verification\nThe fixed code (submission_v2.py) successfully passed the\
    \ simple CPU validation phase and is now running the full training evaluation. The monitor script confirmed the code ran for over 300 seconds without crashing, indicating a successful fix.\n\n## Note for Agent\nIf the goal was to perform a hyperparameter sweep over different `gru_hidden_dim` values, that would need to be configured differently in the Ray Tune setup, not in the `_define_hyperparameters()` function itself. The current system expects plain values that it will wrap appropriately.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    # Return a single concrete value for gru_hidden_dim\n    # The system will handle creating multiple trials if needed\n    return {\n\
    \        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5, 'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n        'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'gru_hidden_dim': 256  # Use single value instead of tune.grid_search\n    }\n\n# --- Shared Components ---\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; kernel_size: int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n\
    \    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return h\n\n# --- Main Network (RNN-Only v2 from ID 388) ---\nclass RnnOnlyNetV2(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; gru_hidden_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(d_model=self.d_model, num_blocks=self.num_blocks, dilations=self.dilations,\n                                              kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \n        gru_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_dim))\n        rnn_output_seq = gru_rnn(features_seq)\n        rnn_vec = rnn_output_seq[:, -1, :]\n\n        projected_vec = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model * 2)(rnn_vec)\n\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(projected_vec)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n        return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1 else logits\n\nclass NetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n\
    \        return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    model = RnnOnlyNetV2(d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"), d_model=hparams.get(\"d_model\"), num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"), dilations=hparams.get(\"dilations\"),\n                         kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"), dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"), gru_hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"gru_hidden_dim\"))\n    return NetworkWrapper(model)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off\
    \ network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset\
    \ training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 253729 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\n\
    Task type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0121 |  0.4015  | 0.4015 \n 20  | 0.0113 |  0.4277  | 0.4418 \n 30  | 0.0107 |  0.4609  | 0.4609 \n 40  | 0.0094 |  0.4468  | 0.4609 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 40 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4609 Time:26s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.460876\nTraining time: 35s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n\
    \ 10  | 0.0005 |  0.0698  | 0.0698 \n 20  | 0.0005 |  0.0540  | 0.0761 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 24 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0761 Time:99s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.076080\nTraining time: 107s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.4031 |  0.7723  | 0.7723 \n 20  | 0.1143 |  0.8692  | 0.8862 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 29 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8862 Time:1282s\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.886154\nTraining\
