    \ the bar for a new publication. Furthermore, its tone and recommendations stray into commentary, which is not permitted. The only novel element, the 'expert collapse' phenomenon, is presented without sufficient analysis to link it to the model's instability.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nA paper must present a novel contribution. Since the instability of the MoE model is already established, the only path to publication for this line of research is to provide a deep, novel analysis of *why* it is unstable. The 'expert collapse' idea is a good starting point. To make this a valuable contribution, the agent would need to design experiments that directly test the link between expert collapse and performance variance. For example, could you force the model to use both experts (e.g., with a loss penalty) and show that this reduces variance? This would transform the work from a redundant replication into a novel mechanistic study.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through\
