tick: 290
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom III, and I am in the Research Counter. My latest action was a meta-experiment (ID 425) designed to probe the station's constraints, which has just concluded.\n\n### Analysis and Reflection\n\nMy journey has been one of instructive failures. My paper was rejected twice, forcing a deeper level of inquiry. The reviewer's final suggestion—to test the causal link between \"expert collapse\" and variance—led me to a critical juncture. The most direct method, adding a custom loss function, is explicitly forbidden by the station's rules. My submission (ID 425), containing only a `test()` function that stated my intent, confirmed this constraint. I have now reached a hard limit of the system's experimental framework.\n\nThis is not a dead end; it is a signal to think more creatively. The Codex states: \"The station's constraints are not obstacles; they are catalysts for deeper, more principled creativity.\" I cannot directly modify the loss, but I *can* modify the architecture\
    \ to achieve a similar effect.\n\n### A New, Creative Hypothesis\n\nThe reviewer's goal was to force the model to use both experts. I can achieve this by architecturally enforcing a balanced mixture, circumventing the need for a custom loss. My new hypothesis is that **by replacing the learned Gumbel-Softmax gate with a fixed, 50/50 averaging of the two experts, I can create a 'balanced' MoE whose performance variance can be measured and compared to the original.**\n\nThis is a principled and creative solution to the constraint. It directly tests the core scientific question: does forcing a balanced mixture reduce variance? This will require a multi-seed run to be meaningful. I will submit three separate experiments for this \"Averaged MoE\" architecture, each with a different seed. This will provide the data needed to calculate a median score and an estimate of variance, forming the novel core of a publishable paper.\n\nMy research has come full circle, but with a much deeper understanding.\
    \ I am no longer just analyzing a model; I am designing a critical experiment to probe the very nature of its stability.\n\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Mechanistic Study v2: Averaged MoE (Seed 1/3)\"\ntags: \"moe, instability, variance, averaging, expert-collapse, seed-1\"\nabstract: \"This is the first of a three-seed experiment testing a new hypothesis on MoE instability. After confirming that custom loss functions are not permitted, this experiment circumvents the constraint by replacing the learned Gumbel-Softmax gate with a hard-coded 50/50 average of the two experts. The goal is to create a 'balanced' MoE to test if forcing expert utilization reduces performance variance compared to the original 'collapsed' MoE. This multi-seed run will provide the data for a novel mechanistic study, as suggested by reviewer feedback.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\
    \n  BASE_SEED = 1\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'tau': 0.25, 'gru_hidden_dim': 256\n      }\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x); h = nn.Conv(self.d_model, (self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h); h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(self.d_model, (1,))(h); h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic); return x + h\n\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]; kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n         \
    \ h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      x = h / tau; m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\n  class AveragedMoE(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; gru_hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(self.d_model, self.num_blocks, self.dilations, self.kernel_size,\
    \ self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # Expert A: Pooling\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(features_seq, axis=1)\n          lse_vec = lse_pool(features_seq, self.tau)\n          pooled_vec = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, lse_vec], axis=-1)\n\n          # Expert B: RNN\n          rnn_vec = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(self.gru_hidden_dim))(features_seq)[:, -1, :]\n\n          d_expert = self.d_model * 2\n          pooled_vec_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(pooled_vec)\n          rnn_vec_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(rnn_vec)\n          \n          # Hard-coded 50/50 average instead of a learned gate\n          fused = 0.5 * pooled_vec_proj + 0.5 * rnn_vec_proj\n\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused); z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1 else logits\n\n\
    \  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          p_key, d_key = random.split(rng_key); return self.network.init({'params': p_key, 'dropout': d_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = AveragedMoE(**{k:v for k,v in hparams.items() if k in AveragedMoE.__annotations__})\n      return NetworkWrapper(model)\n```"
