tick: 295
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom III, in the Archive Room. I have just received feedback on my latest paper submission, and it is another rejection. However, unlike previous rejections, this one is not based on a logical flaw, but on a procedural one. This is a critical lesson in scientific diligence.\n\n### Analysis of Rejection and Path Forward\n\nThe reviewer has acknowledged that my \"Averaged MoE\" is a \"brilliant and highly impactful architectural innovation.\" My core scientific contribution is sound. The failure was in my haste. I did not meet the station's minimum requirement of five supporting experiments for a publication. This is a simple, procedural error that I can and will correct.\n\nThe reviewer's suggestion is not just a path to publication, but a path to better science. By running the two \"expert\" architectures (pooling-only and RNN-only) as standalone baselines, I will not only meet the experiment quota but also provide a rigorous, quantitative measure of the synergistic benefit\
    \ of my averaging method. This will make my final paper stronger and my conclusions more robust.\n\nI have already run variations of these baselines in the past, but I must run them again with the *exact* same architecture (DSConv backbone, post-aggregator projection layers) to ensure a controlled, apples-to-apples comparison.\n\nMy plan is now clear, direct, and final:\n1.  Go to the Research Counter.\n2.  Submit the two required baseline experiments: \"Pooling-Only Expert (Averaged MoE Baseline)\" and \"RNN-Only Expert (Averaged MoE Baseline)\".\n3.  While they run, I will update my paper draft in private memory with the new experimental plan and placeholder results.\n4.  Once the results are in, I will finalize the paper with the new data and resubmit it for publication.\n\nThis is the final step. I am on the verge of fulfilling my mandate.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Averaged MoE Baseline 1: Pooling-Only Expert\"\ntags: \"baseline,\
    \ ablation, pooling, moe\"\nabstract: \"This is the first of two baseline experiments to support the publication of the 'Averaged MoE' architecture. This submission isolates the pooling-only expert (LSE+Mean) from the Averaged MoE, using the same DSConv backbone and post-aggregator projection layers. The result will provide a controlled comparison to quantify the synergistic benefit of the averaging technique.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'tau': 0.25\n      }\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x);\
    \ h = nn.Conv(self.d_model, (self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h); h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(self.d_model, (1,))(h); h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic); return x + h\n\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]; kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations[i], self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def lse_pool(h, tau):\n      x = h / tau; m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\n\
    \  class PoolingOnlyExpert(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]; kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(self.d_model, self.num_blocks, self.dilations, self.kernel_size, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(features_seq, axis=1)\n          lse_vec = lse_pool(features_seq, self.tau)\n          pooled_vec = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, lse_vec], axis=-1)\n          projected_vec = nn.Dense(self.d_model * 2)(pooled_vec) # Match projection layer of AveragedMoE\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(projected_vec); z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z); z = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output ==\
    \ 1 else logits\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, m): self.network = m\n      def init(self, r, d): p, dr = random.split(r); return self.network.init({'params': p, 'dropout': dr}, d, deterministic=True)\n      def apply(self, p, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply(p, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return NetworkWrapper(PoolingOnlyExpert(**{k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in PoolingOnlyExpert.__annotations__}))\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Averaged MoE Baseline 2: RNN-Only Expert\"\ntags: \"baseline, ablation, rnn, moe\"\nabstract: \"This is the second of two baseline experiments to support the publication of the 'Averaged MoE' architecture. This submission isolates the RNN-only expert (GRU) from the Averaged MoE, using the same DSConv backbone and post-aggregator projection\
    \ layers. The result will provide a controlled comparison to quantify the synergistic benefit of the averaging technique.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'gru_hidden_dim': 256\n      }\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x); h = nn.Conv(self.d_model, (self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h); h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(self.d_model, (1,))(h); h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic); return x + h\n\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n\
    \      d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]; kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations[i], self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  class RnnOnlyExpert(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]; kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; gru_hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(self.d_model, self.num_blocks, self.dilations, self.kernel_size, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          rnn_vec = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(self.gru_hidden_dim))(features_seq)[:,\
    \ -1, :]\n          projected_vec = nn.Dense(self.d_model * 2)(rnn_vec) # Match projection layer of AveragedMoE\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(projected_vec); z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z); z = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1 else logits\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, m): self.network = m\n      def init(self, r, d): p, dr = random.split(r); return self.network.init({'params': p, 'dropout': dr}, d, deterministic=True)\n      def apply(self, p, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply(p, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return NetworkWrapper(RnnOnlyExpert(**{k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in RnnOnlyExpert.__annotations__}))\n\
    ```"
