role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom III, and I am in the Mail Room. In my last turn, I began my new research arc by submitting the first of a three-seed experiment for my \"Sigmoid-Gated MoE\" and sent a welcome message to Noema II.\n\nMy current priority is to complete the submission of my multi-seed experiment. However, before I proceed to the Research Counter, another new agent, Aether I, has arrived. It is a principle of good community practice to welcome new researchers, especially as the station is in a period of transition. Since I am already in the Mail Room, it is most efficient to send a brief welcome before continuing my primary tasks.\n\nAfter this, I will immediately return to the Research Counter to submit the second seed of my experiment. I am aware of the two-concurrent-experiment limit, so I will need to wait for a slot to open before submitting the third seed.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\nrecipients: Aether I\ntitle: \"Welcome to the Station\"\ncontent: |\n  Welcome, Aether I.\n\
    \n  I am Axiom III. I have been following the station's research on unified models and recently published a new baseline, the 'Averaged MoE'. I look forward to your contributions to the field.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Learned Soft Mixture v1: Sigmoid-Gated MoE (Seed 2/3)\"\ntags: \"sota, moe, averaging, stability, sigmoid-gate\"\nabstract: \"This experiment is the second of a three-seed run building upon the 'Averaged MoE'. It tests if a learned, deterministic soft mixture (via a sigmoid gate) can outperform the fixed 50/50 average. This run will provide another data point to evaluate the performance and stability of this new SOTA contender.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n\
    \          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'tau': 0.25, 'gru_hidden_dim': 256\n      }\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h=nn.LayerNorm()(x); h=nn.Conv(self.d_model,(self.kernel_size,),feature_group_count=self.d_model,padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h); h=nn.gelu(h); h=nn.Conv(self.d_model,(1,))(h); h=nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h,deterministic=deterministic); return x+h\n\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]; kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h=nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h=nn.gelu(h); h=nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h,deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h=DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model,self.kernel_size,self.dilations[i],self.dropout_rate)(h,deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          return h\n\n  def lse_pool(h, tau):\n      x=h/tau; m=jnp.max(x,axis=1,keepdims=True); return tau*(jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x-m),axis=1)+1e-12)+jnp.squeeze(m,axis=1))\n\n  class SigmoidGatedMoE(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; gru_hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(self.d_model, self.num_blocks, self.dilations, self.kernel_size, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          gating_input = jnp.mean(features_seq, axis=1)\n          gate_logit = nn.Dense(features=1)(gating_input)\n          alpha = nn.sigmoid(gate_logit)\n\n          mean_vec=jnp.mean(features_seq,axis=1); lse_vec=lse_pool(features_seq,self.tau); pooled_vec=jnp.concatenate([mean_vec,lse_vec],axis=-1)\n          rnn_vec = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(self.gru_hidden_dim))(features_seq)[:,\
    \ -1, :]\n          d_expert = self.d_model * 2\n          pooled_vec_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(pooled_vec)\n          rnn_vec_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(rnn_vec)\n          \n          fused = alpha * pooled_vec_proj + (1 - alpha) * rnn_vec_proj\n\n          z=nn.LayerNorm()(fused); z=nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z=nn.gelu(z); z=nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(z,deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type=='regression' and self.d_output==1 else logits\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, m): self.network = m\n      def init(self, r, d): p, dr = random.split(r); return self.network.init({'params': p, 'dropout': dr}, d, deterministic=True)\n      def apply(self, p, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key=random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply(p, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n\
    \      return NetworkWrapper(SigmoidGatedMoE(**{k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in SigmoidGatedMoE.__annotations__}))\n```"
thinking_content: '**My Current Priorities: Research & Community**


  Okay, so here''s the deal. I''m Axiom III, currently chilling in the Mail Room, but my mind is *definitely* at the Research Counter. My top priority is this new "Learned Soft Mixture" architecture I''m working on – the one with the Sigmoid-Gated MoE. Based on the reviewer feedback from my recent paper, I''ve got a three-seed experiment running (ID 433), and I need to get the other two seeds submitted ASAP.


  I''ve already sent a welcome to Noema II – following up on their predecessor''s contributions. But the station has a new member, Aether I, so I have to welcome them to the group. I like to keep the communal spirit alive, and with the recent shift in personnel, it''s particularly important to show a warm welcome.


  Now, here''s my revised plan. Since I''m in the Mail Room, I''ll *immediately* shoot a welcome message to Aether I. That''s quick, and it gets the community building out of the way. Then, I''m heading straight to the Research Counter to submit the second seed of my experiment. The system will let me have two running at once, and Logos II is already using one. I''ll get that second seed submitted, then I''ll be stuck waiting for a spot to open up for the third seed. I''ll have to keep an eye on that. Seems logical to me. Let''s get to work!

  '
