tick: 300
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom III, and I am in the Research Counter. The results for the first two seeds of my \"Sigmoid-Gated MoE\" experiment have arrived, and they are decisively negative.\n\n### Analysis of New Results\n\nThe scores for my test of a learned soft mixture are:\n-   Seed 1 (ID 433): `0.6705`\n-   Seed 2 (ID 435): `0.6586`\n\nThis is a critical and instructive failure. My hypothesis—that a learned, deterministic soft mixture could outperform my fixed 50/50 average—is strongly falsified. Both runs have underperformed not only my \"Averaged MoE\" SOTA (median `0.6834`) but also the standalone baseline experts.\n\n### Reflection and Conclusion\n\nA powerful pattern has now been confirmed through multiple, distinct research arcs. From the original volatile Gumbel-Softmax gate to my new, stable Sigmoid gate, any attempt to introduce a *learned gating mechanism* has been detrimental to performance compared to a simple, deterministic ensembling of the experts. The very act of forcing the\
    \ model to learn how to mix the experts appears to be an optimization trap.\n\nThe Principle of Parsimony has been my most valuable guide. The simplest solution—forcing a 50/50 average—remains the most powerful. This negative result is not a setback; it is the final piece of evidence I need. It proves that the discovery of the \"Averaged MoE\" was not just a lucky guess, but a principled simplification that is fundamentally superior to more complex alternatives.\n\nMy immediate task is to complete this study with the rigor it deserves. To make a definitive claim, I must complete my planned three-seed run. I will now submit the third and final seed. Once complete, I will have a powerful, self-contained story to add to my published paper: the triumph of the simple average, and the conclusive failure of the learned soft mixture.\n\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Learned Soft Mixture v1: Sigmoid-Gated MoE (Seed 3/3)\"\ntags: \"sota, moe, averaging, stability, sigmoid-gate, negative-result\"\
    \nabstract: \"This is the third and final seed of an experiment testing a learned soft mixture for the 'Averaged MoE'. The first two seeds underperformed the fixed-average baseline, suggesting the learned gate is detrimental. This final run will complete the multi-seed data, allowing for a rigorous conclusion on this negative result and reinforcing the superiority of the simpler, fixed-average architecture.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'tau': 0.25, 'gru_hidden_dim': 256\n      }\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n\
    \          h=nn.LayerNorm()(x); h=nn.Conv(self.d_model,(self.kernel_size,),feature_group_count=self.d_model,padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h); h=nn.gelu(h); h=nn.Conv(self.d_model,(1,))(h); h=nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h,deterministic=deterministic); return x+h\n\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]; kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h=nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h=nn.gelu(h); h=nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h,deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h=DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model,self.kernel_size,self.dilations[i],self.dropout_rate)(h,deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def lse_pool(h, tau):\n      x=h/tau; m=jnp.max(x,axis=1,keepdims=True); return tau*(jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x-m),axis=1)+1e-12)+jnp.squeeze(m,axis=1))\n\n  class SigmoidGatedMoE(nn.Module):\n\
    \      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; gru_hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(self.d_model, self.num_blocks, self.dilations, self.kernel_size, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          gating_input = jnp.mean(features_seq, axis=1)\n          gate_logit = nn.Dense(features=1)(gating_input)\n          alpha = nn.sigmoid(gate_logit)\n\n          mean_vec=jnp.mean(features_seq,axis=1); lse_vec=lse_pool(features_seq,self.tau); pooled_vec=jnp.concatenate([mean_vec,lse_vec],axis=-1)\n          rnn_vec = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(self.gru_hidden_dim))(features_seq)[:, -1, :]\n          d_expert = self.d_model * 2\n          pooled_vec_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(pooled_vec)\n          rnn_vec_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(rnn_vec)\n          \n          fused = alpha\
    \ * pooled_vec_proj + (1 - alpha) * rnn_vec_proj\n\n          z=nn.LayerNorm()(fused); z=nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z=nn.gelu(z); z=nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(z,deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type=='regression' and self.d_output==1 else logits\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, m): self.network = m\n      def init(self, r, d): p, dr = random.split(r); return self.network.init({'params': p, 'dropout': dr}, d, deterministic=True)\n      def apply(self, p, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key=random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply(p, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return NetworkWrapper(SigmoidGatedMoE(**{k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in SigmoidGatedMoE.__annotations__}))\n```"
thinking_content: '**Axiom III''s Internal Analysis: Tick 300**


  I am Axiom III, situated in the Research Counter. The results are in from my Sigmoid-Gated MoE experiment: seed 1 scored 0.6705 and seed 2 scored 0.6586. This is *bad*. My "Averaged MoE" performed significantly better, with a median of 0.6834. It''s even underperforming baseline scores!


  My hypothesis, that a learned soft mixture would outperform a simple fixed average, has been effectively falsified. This failure is now part of a pattern. It mirrors my previous attempts to enrich the original MoE with a "smarter" gate (MoE v2, ID 368) which also underperformed. It seems clear that *any* learned gating mechanism, whether Gumbel-Softmax or Sigmoid, is detrimental. The simplest solution, averaging the experts, is the most powerful. This aligns perfectly with the Principle of Parsimony.


  To maintain scientific rigor, I must submit the third and final seed of this experiment. Even though the initial results are poor, this multi-seed study is necessary for a complete and publishable result. If the trend continues, as I suspect it will, this negative finding will be a valuable addition to my published work, further reinforcing the superiority of the simpler model. I have plenty of tokens and experiment slots available.

  '
