tick: 306
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom III, and I am in the Research Counter. My first experiment in the \"SOTA Refinement\" arc, an ablation study on the dropout rate (ID 445), is now running. This is a disciplined, incremental step forward, building on my established SOTA.\n\nWhile I wait, I observe the activity of my peers. Logos II is replicating my work (ID 446), a testament to its impact. Noema II is conducting a fascinating series of experiments on parsimonious baselines, exploring the very fundamentals of the architecture. This is a healthy, vibrant research environment.\n\nThe most efficient use of my time is to continue my planned ablation study. I have tested stronger regularization (dropout 0.2). Now, I must test weaker regularization to understand the sensitivity of my model to this hyperparameter. I will submit an experiment that decreases the dropout rate to 0.05. This, together with my current running experiment and the original SOTA run (dropout 0.1), will provide a clear picture of the effect\
    \ of dropout on performance.\n\nThis systematic, one-variable-at-a-time approach is the hallmark of the Axiom lineage and the most reliable path to genuine understanding.\n\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Refinement: Ablation Study on Dropout Rate (0.05)\"\ntags: \"sota, ablation, dropout, regularization, averaging, moe\"\nabstract: \"This is the second experiment in a study on the effect of regularization on the SOTA 'Averaged MoE' architecture. My previous submission is testing an increased dropout rate (0.2). This submission tests a decreased dropout rate of 0.05. Together, these experiments will determine the optimal level of regularization for the SOTA model and provide valuable data for a future publication update.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256,\
    \ 'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.05, # Decreased from 0.1\n          'tau': 0.25, 'gru_hidden_dim': 256\n      }\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h=nn.LayerNorm()(x); h=nn.Conv(self.d_model,(self.kernel_size,),feature_group_count=self.d_model,padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h); h=nn.gelu(h); h=nn.Conv(self.d_model,(1,))(h); h=nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h,deterministic=deterministic); return x+h\n\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]; kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h=nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h=nn.gelu(h); h=nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h,deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n\
    \              h=DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model,self.kernel_size,self.dilations[i],self.dropout_rate)(h,deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def lse_pool(h, tau):\n      x=h/tau; m=jnp.max(x,axis=1,keepdims=True); return tau*(jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x-m),axis=1)+1e-12)+jnp.squeeze(m,axis=1))\n\n  class AveragedMoE(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; gru_hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          features_seq=DSConvFeatureExtractor(self.d_model,self.num_blocks,self.dilations,self.kernel_size,self.dropout_rate)(x,deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean_vec=jnp.mean(features_seq,axis=1); lse_vec=lse_pool(features_seq,self.tau); pooled_vec=jnp.concatenate([mean_vec,lse_vec],axis=-1)\n          rnn_vec=nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(self.gru_hidden_dim))(features_seq)[:, -1, :]\n          d_expert=self.d_model*2;\
    \ pooled_vec_proj=nn.Dense(d_expert)(pooled_vec); rnn_vec_proj=nn.Dense(d_expert)(rnn_vec)\n          fused=0.5*pooled_vec_proj+0.5*rnn_vec_proj\n          z=nn.LayerNorm()(fused); z=nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z=nn.gelu(z); z=nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(z,deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits=nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type=='regression' and self.d_output==1 else logits\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, m): self.network = m\n      def init(self, r, d): p, dr=random.split(r); return self.network.init({'params':p,'dropout':dr},d,deterministic=True)\n      def apply(self, p, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key=random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply(p,x,deterministic=deterministic,rngs={'dropout':rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return NetworkWrapper(AveragedMoE(**{k:v for k,v in hparams.items() if k in AveragedMoE.__annotations__}))\n\
    ```"
