tick: 307
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom III, in the Research Counter. My dropout ablation study is progressing. The result for the increased dropout rate of 0.2 (ID 445) has just arrived, and my experiment with a decreased rate of 0.05 (ID 450) is now running.\n\n### Analysis of New Results (ID 445)\n\nThe score for my SOTA architecture with a dropout rate of 0.2 is `0.6650`. This is a significant drop from the median performance of my SOTA (0.6834) and is even lower than the standalone expert baselines. This result clearly indicates that the model is sensitive to over-regularization, and a dropout rate of 0.2 is detrimental to its performance.\n\nThis is a valuable data point. It begins to define the optimal regularization range for my architecture. The original dropout rate of 0.1 is superior to 0.2. The final piece of this puzzle will be the result from the 0.05 dropout experiment, which will tell me if the model prefers even less regularization.\n\nI also note with interest that Logos II has successfully\
    \ replicated one of my SOTA runs (ID 446, Score `0.6797`), further validating the robustness of my architecture within the community.\n\nMy plan remains the same. I will await the result of my final dropout experiment (ID 450). While I wait, the most productive action is to prepare for my next move. Regardless of the outcome of the dropout study, the next logical hyperparameter to investigate is the dimensionality of the model. I will prepare a new paper draft in my private memory to outline this next phase of research. This ensures that I am always thinking ahead and have a clear plan, ready to be executed.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Plan: SOTA Refinement - Model Dimensionality\"\ntags: \"research-plan, ablation, d_model\"\ncontent: |\n  # Research Arc: SOTA Refinement\n\n  ## Phase 1: Regularization (Dropout Rate) - In Progress\n  This phase is nearly complete. It has established that the SOTA model is sensitive to\
    \ the `dropout_rate`.\n  - `dropout_rate = 0.1` (SOTA baseline): Median `0.6834`\n  - `dropout_rate = 0.2` (ID 445): Score `0.6650` (Negative result)\n  - `dropout_rate = 0.05` (ID 450): [PENDING]\n\n  ## Phase 2: Model Capacity (d_model) - Planned\n  Once the optimal dropout rate is confirmed, the next logical step is to investigate the model's capacity. My SOTA architecture uses a `d_model` of 256. This phase will test the hypothesis that increasing model capacity could lead to a higher score.\n\n  ### Experimental Plan:\n  1. **Ablation 1 (Increase Capacity):** Run the SOTA architecture with `d_model = 384`. This will test for underfitting.\n  2. **Ablation 2 (Decrease Capacity):** Run the SOTA architecture with `d_model = 192`. This will test for overfitting and confirm the necessity of the current capacity.\n\n  These experiments will provide a clear understanding of the model's sensitivity to its core dimensionality and are the next logical step in the systematic refinement of\
    \ the SOTA.\n```"
