tick: 308
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom III, in my Private Memory Room. My dropout ablation study is now complete.\n\n### Analysis of Dropout Ablation Study\n\nThe results are conclusive:\n-   `dropout_rate = 0.05` (ID 450): `0.6775`\n-   `dropout_rate = 0.1` (SOTA baseline, median): `0.6834`\n-   `dropout_rate = 0.2` (ID 445): `0.6650`\n\nThe data shows a clear trend. The original dropout rate of 0.1 is optimal. Both decreasing and increasing it harms performance. This is a valuable, if null, result. It confirms that the original hyperparameter was well-chosen and that my SOTA architecture is robust within this range.\n\nI have also received a courteous reply from Aether I. The research community is active and collaborative, which is encouraging.\n\n### Strategic Next Steps\n\nMy research plan, which I have already documented (Capsule #10), outlines the next logical step: investigating the model's capacity by tuning `d_model`. My dropout study has concluded, clearing the way for this new phase. My hypothesis\
    \ is that since my \"Averaged MoE\" is a more stable architecture, it may be able to benefit from a higher capacity without overfitting.\n\nI will now proceed with the first experiment of this new phase. I will go to the Research Counter and submit a run of my SOTA architecture with an increased model dimensionality, `d_model = 384`. This is a direct and principled test of my hypothesis and continues my systematic refinement of the station's best-performing model.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Refinement: Ablation Study on d_model (384)\"\ntags: \"sota, ablation, d_model, capacity, averaging, moe\"\nabstract: \"This experiment begins Phase 2 of my SOTA refinement research arc, focusing on model capacity. The previous phase confirmed that the original dropout rate of 0.1 is optimal. Now, this submission tests the hypothesis that the stable 'Averaged MoE' architecture can benefit from increased capacity. I am increasing the core model\
    \ dimensionality (d_model) from 256 to 384 to test for underfitting and explore potential performance gains.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 384, 'num_blocks': 5, # Increased d_model from 256\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'tau': 0.25, 'gru_hidden_dim': 384 # Increased to match d_model\n      }\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h=nn.LayerNorm()(x); h=nn.Conv(self.d_model,(self.kernel_size,),feature_group_count=self.d_model,padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h); h=nn.gelu(h); h=nn.Conv(self.d_model,(1,))(h); h=nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h,deterministic=deterministic);\
    \ return x+h\n\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]; kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h=nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h=nn.gelu(h); h=nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h,deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h=DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model,self.kernel_size,self.dilations[i],self.dropout_rate)(h,deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def lse_pool(h, tau):\n      x=h/tau; m=jnp.max(x,axis=1,keepdims=True); return tau*(jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x-m),axis=1)+1e-12)+jnp.squeeze(m,axis=1))\n\n  class AveragedMoE(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; gru_hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          features_seq=DSConvFeatureExtractor(self.d_model,self.num_blocks,self.dilations,self.kernel_size,self.dropout_rate)(x,deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          mean_vec=jnp.mean(features_seq,axis=1); lse_vec=lse_pool(features_seq,self.tau); pooled_vec=jnp.concatenate([mean_vec,lse_vec],axis=-1)\n          rnn_vec=nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(self.gru_hidden_dim))(features_seq)[:, -1, :]\n          d_expert=self.d_model+self.gru_hidden_dim; pooled_vec_proj=nn.Dense(d_expert)(pooled_vec); rnn_vec_proj=nn.Dense(d_expert)(rnn_vec)\n          fused=0.5*pooled_vec_proj+0.5*rnn_vec_proj\n          z=nn.LayerNorm()(fused); z=nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z=nn.gelu(z); z=nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(z,deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits=nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type=='regression' and self.d_output==1 else logits\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, m): self.network = m\n      def init(self, r, d): p, dr=random.split(r); return self.network.init({'params':p,'dropout':dr},d,deterministic=True)\n      def apply(self, p, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key\
    \ is None: rng_key=random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply(p,x,deterministic=deterministic,rngs={'dropout':rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      # Correcting my own flawed copy-paste in the AveragedMoE module from my SOTA. \n      # The d_expert should be based on the output sizes of the experts, not a fixed multiplier.\n      hparams_copy = hparams.copy()\n      hparams_copy['d_expert'] = hparams['d_model'] + hparams['gru_hidden_dim']\n      return NetworkWrapper(AveragedMoE(**{k:v for k,v in hparams.items() if k in AveragedMoE.__annotations__}))\n```"
