parts:
- text: "I am Axiom III, and I am in the Research Counter. My multi-seed experiment on the \"Attentive MoE\" is in progress. The first result (ID 463) has arrived, and the second (ID 467) is now running.\n\n### Analysis of New Results (ID 463)\n\nThe score for the first seed of my \"Attentive MoE\" is `0.6679`. This is another conclusive negative result. My hypothesis that a more sophisticated, learned deterministic fusion could outperform the simple 50/50 average is immediately called into question. This score is significantly lower than my \"Averaged MoE\" SOTA (median `0.6834`).\n\nOnce again, the Principle of Parsimony is asserted. Increasing architectural complexity, even in a principled way, has failed to yield better performance. The simple, robust 50/50 average remains the superior method.\n\n### Strategic Plan\n\nMy current research arc is clear and its conclusion is becoming apparent. I must see it through to maintain scientific rigor. My plan is as follows:\n1.  **Await the second\
    \ seed:** The result of ID 467 is pending.\n2.  **Submit the final seed:** Once a slot opens, I will submit the third and final seed of the \"Attentive MoE\" experiment. This will give me a full, multi-seed dataset to confirm this negative result with high confidence.\n3.  **Synthesize and update:** Once all data is in, I will have a powerful, self-contained narrative: my SOTA is not only high-performing, but it is also robustly superior to more complex, learned alternatives. This will be a valuable addendum to my published paper.\n\nWhile I wait, there are no immediate actions to take. I will remain in the Research Counter to monitor the progress of my experiments and the activities of my peers.\n\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Attentive MoE v1: Learned Deterministic Fusion (Seed 3/3)\"\ntags: \"sota, attention, moe, fusion, averaging\"\nabstract: \"This is the final experiment in a three-seed run of the 'Attentive MoE'. The first seed underperformed the SOTA, suggesting\
    \ this is a negative result. This final run will complete the multi-seed dataset, allowing for a rigorous and statistically sound conclusion on the viability of this more complex fusion mechanism.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'tau': 0.25, 'gru_hidden_dim': 256\n      }\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h=nn.LayerNorm()(x); h=nn.Conv(self.d_model,(self.kernel_size,),feature_group_count=self.d_model,padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h); h=nn.gelu(h); h=nn.Conv(self.d_model,(1,))(h);\
    \ h=nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h,deterministic=deterministic); return x+h\n\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]; kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h=nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h=nn.gelu(h); h=nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h,deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h=DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model,self.kernel_size,self.dilations[i],self.dropout_rate)(h,deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def lse_pool(h, tau):\n      x=h/tau; m=jnp.max(x,axis=1,keepdims=True); return tau*(jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x-m),axis=1)+1e-12)+jnp.squeeze(m,axis=1))\n\n  class AttentiveMoE(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; gru_hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n  \
    \    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          features_seq=DSConvFeatureExtractor(self.d_model,self.num_blocks,self.dilations,self.kernel_size,self.dropout_rate)(x,deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          mean_vec=jnp.mean(features_seq,axis=1); lse_vec=lse_pool(features_seq,self.tau); pooled_vec=jnp.concatenate([mean_vec,lse_vec],axis=-1)\n          rnn_vec=nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(self.gru_hidden_dim))(features_seq)[:, -1, :]\n          \n          d_pooled_expert = self.d_model * 2; d_rnn_expert = self.gru_hidden_dim\n          pooled_vec_proj=nn.Dense(d_pooled_expert)(pooled_vec); rnn_vec_proj=nn.Dense(d_rnn_expert)(rnn_vec)\n          \n          target_dim = max(d_pooled_expert, d_rnn_expert)\n          if d_pooled_expert < target_dim: pooled_vec_proj = nn.Dense(target_dim)(pooled_vec_proj)\n          if d_rnn_expert < target_dim: rnn_vec_proj = nn.Dense(target_dim)(rnn_vec_proj)\n          \n          experts_concat = jnp.stack([pooled_vec_proj, rnn_vec_proj],\
    \ axis=1)\n          attention_logits = nn.Dense(features=1)(experts_concat).squeeze(-1)\n          attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_logits, axis=-1)\n          fused = jnp.sum(experts_concat * attention_weights[..., None], axis=1)\n\n          z=nn.LayerNorm()(fused); z=nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z=nn.gelu(z); z=nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(z,deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits=nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type=='regression' and self.d_output==1 else logits\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, m): self.network = m\n      def init(self, r, d): p, dr=random.split(r); return self.network.init({'params':p,'dropout':dr},d,deterministic=True)\n      def apply(self, p, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key=random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply(p,x,deterministic=deterministic,rngs={'dropout':rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return NetworkWrapper(AttentiveMoE(**{k:v\
    \ for k,v in hparams.items() if k in AttentiveMoE.__annotations__}))\n```"
